At the start, the need for reduction was estimated to be approximately 380 employees.
With the reduction of the population, the aim is to achieve annual cost savings of approximately 20 million euros, which are scheduled to materialise during the next year.
Stockmann has previously started an efficiency programme, which aims to achieve savings of 50 million euros this year.
This is due to Stockmann's difficulties in obtaining profitability from department store sales.
Although the Group's adjusted operating result improved to 11.1 million euros in the second quarter, department store sales are still making losses.
According to Stockmann's acting CEO Lauri Veijalainen, sales in department stores have not reached the company's targets.
"Unfortunately, personnel reductions are necessary to ensure Stockmann Retail's positive operating result in 2018," Veijalainen says in a press release.
The result improvement in the second quarter was mainly due to the success of the clothing chain Lindex.
Ketju achieved its all-as-the-best second-quarter net sales and results.
Lindex's operating profit increased by MEUR 9.5 to 28.1 million euros.
In the corresponding period last year, Stockmann Group's operating result was 4.1 million negative.
Stockmann estimates that the Group's net sales for this year will decrease from last year.
The adjusted operating result is expected to be slightly positive this year.
