Up to a third of the state's total tax revenue would not be received if Donald Trump's shift to corporate tax was implemented.
Tax revenues would also decrease, in particular, due to tax incentives that benefit the richest.
Trump described his tax program as a revolution when he presented it in Detroit on Monday.
Corporate tax would fall from 35% to 15 percent.
I wouldn't collect a huge amount, 1 000 billion dollars a year.
