Hindes was narrowly lagging behind, but Kenny pushed into the team's lead and Skinner held on to it.
The strategy change was a big part of the makeover, and it included Hindes driving in bigger gear to slow down and allow Kenny, and Skinner in particular, to hold on to the pace.
